From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:14:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Start map_reserved_area()'s top-down search at
 limit_low.

The top-down branch took a reserved area's own start as the lower bound
of the space it fits the view into, so a view could be placed below
limit_low when the area extended below it: a 64 KiB top-down
reservation bounded to a 48 KiB window of the macOS soft pagezero came
back below the window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 2f96a37..b69301d 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -1839,7 +1839,7 @@ static void *map_reserved_area( void *limit_low, void *limit_high, size_t size,
         for (area = find_mem_area( end ); end > limit_low; end = mem_area_end( --area ))
         {
             if (mem_area_state( area ) != AREA_RESERVED) continue;
-            start = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)mem_area_base( area ) + align_mask, align_mask );
+            start = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)max( mem_area_base( area ), limit_low ) + align_mask, align_mask );
             if (start >= end || (char *)end - (char *)start < size) continue;
             ptr = ROUND_ADDR( (char *)end - size, align_mask );
             break;
